{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the land became defiled, and I visited its iniquity upon it, and the land vomited</b>. Scripture was stringent concerning forbidden sexual relations, because the land becomes defiled through them and vomits out the souls that commit them. Now forbidden sexual relations are an obligation of the body and are not dependent upon the land, but the secret of the matter in Scripture is what it says (Deuteronomy 32:8–9): \"When the Most High gave nations their inheritance, when He separated the children of man, He set the boundaries of the peoples,\" etc., \"For the portion of YHWH is His people,\" etc. The meaning is that HaShem the glorious created everything, and placed the power of the lower beings in the upper ones, and assigned over every nation in their lands, for their peoples, a known star and constellation, as is known in astrology. This is what is said (Deuteronomy 4:19): \"which YHWH your Elohim has allotted to all the peoples,\" for He allotted to all of them constellations in the heavens, and higher than them are angels of the Most High, appointed to be officers over them, as it is written (Daniel 10:13): \"and the prince of the kingdom of Persia stood against me,\" and it is written (ibid. v. 20): \"and the prince of Greece is coming,\" and they are called \"kings,\" as it is written (ibid. v. 13): \"and I was left there beside the kings of Persia.\" Now HaShem the glorious is Elohim of the elohim and Adonai of the adonim over the entire world, but the land of Israel, the middle of the inhabited world, is the inheritance of YHWH uniquely dedicated to His name; He did not appoint over it any angelic officer, magistrate, or ruler, when He gave it as an inheritance to His people who declare His unity, the seed of His beloved. This is what He says (Exodus 19:5): \"and you shall be to Me a treasure from all the peoples, for all the earth is Mine,\" and it is written (Jeremiah 11:4): \"and you shall be to Me for a people, and I shall be to you for an Elohim\" — not that you shall belong to other elohim at all. He sanctified the people dwelling in His land through the holiness of forbidden relations and the multiplicity of commandments, to be for His name. Therefore He said (Leviticus 20:22): \"and you shall keep all My statutes and all My ordinances and do them, and the land shall not vomit you out,\" and it is written (ibid. v. 24): \"and I said to you, you shall possess their land, and I shall give it to you to possess it, I am YHWH your Elohim who has separated you from the peoples\" — He says that He separated us from all the peoples over whom He appointed officers and other elohim, by giving us the land, so that He, blessed be He, shall be to us for an Elohim and we shall be uniquely dedicated to His name. Now the land, which is the inheritance of HaShem the glorious, vomits out all who defile it, and it cannot tolerate idolaters and those who uncover forbidden relations. This parashah mentioned Molech, to include idolatry together with the remembrance of forbidden relations, and concerning all of them He said (here): \"Do not defile yourselves in all of these, for in all of these the nations were defiled, and the land vomited out its inhabitants.\" Likewise He said in the second parashah (Leviticus 20:26): \"and I separated you from the peoples to be Mine,\" which is a stringency of the prohibition of idolatry. Therefore He said that because they are uniquely dedicated to His name, for that reason He gave them the land, as it is said (ibid. v. 24): \"and I said to you, you shall possess their land, and I shall give it to you to possess it, I am YHWH your Elohim who has separated you from the peoples.\" Now outside the Land, even though everything belongs to HaShem the glorious, purity is not complete there, because of the ministering angels who rule over it, and the peoples stray after their officers to worship even them. Therefore Scripture says (Isaiah 54:5): \"the Elohim of all the earth shall He be called,\" for He is Elohim of the elohim who rules over all, and He will ultimately punish the host of the height in the height (ibid. 24:21), to remove the dominion of the celestial beings and to destroy the array of the ministering angels, and afterwards He will punish the kings of the earth on the earth (ibid.). This is the meaning of what Scripture says (Daniel 4:14): \"by the decree of the watchers is the matter, and by the word of the holy ones is the question\" — He says that the matter decreed upon Nebuchadnezzar is a decree of the watchers, which the forces emanated from them decreed to do thus, and they are called \"watchers\" because from their emanation the powers are aroused in all actions, as He said (ibid. 4:10): \"and behold, a watcher and a holy one came down from heaven and cried aloud,\" and thus he said: \"Hew down the tree,\" etc. \"And by the word of the holy ones is the question,\" meaning that they asked what the supernal will was concerning him, and afterwards they decreed that it be done. This is what Daniel said to him (ibid. v. 21): \"and it is a decree of the Most High,\" for everything is from Him, blessed be He. Now HaShem the glorious, blessed be He, is Elohim of the elohim outside the Land, and the Elohim of the land of Israel, which is the inheritance of YHWH. This is the reason for \"and she shall go astray after the elohim of the stranger of the land\" (Deuteronomy 31:16), for the elohim are strangers in the land of HaShem and in His inheritance. This is what is said (II Kings 17:26): \"they do not know the ordinance of the Elohim of the land, and He sent the lions among them, and behold they are killing them, because they do not know the ordinance of the Elohim of the land.\" Now the Cutheans were not punished in their own land for worshipping their elohim by having lions sent among them, but when they came to the land of HaShem and did there as their former deeds, He sent among them the lions that killed them. So too they taught in Sifra (Kedoshim 11:14): \"and the land shall not vomit you out,\" etc. — the land of Israel is not like other lands; it does not sustain transgressors. And in Sifrei (Ha'azinu 15): \"and there was no strange el with Him\" (Deuteronomy 32:12) — that no nation's officer has authority to come and dominate you, as in the matter that is said: \"and I am going out, and behold the prince of Greece,\" etc. And it is their statement (Ketubot 110b): whoever dwells outside the Land is like one who has no eloah, as it is said (Leviticus 25:38): \"to give you the land of Canaan to be to you for an Elohim,\" and it says (I Samuel 26:19): \"for they have driven me out today from being attached to the inheritance of YHWH, saying, Go, serve other elohim.\" And they said in the Tosefta of Avodah Zarah (ch. 5, hal. 5): behold he says (Genesis 28:21): \"and I shall return in peace to my father's house, and YHWH shall be to me for an Elohim,\" and He says: \"to give you the land of Canaan\" (Leviticus 25:38) — all the time you are in the land of Canaan, I was to you for an Elohim; you are not in the land of Canaan — as it were, I am not to you for an Elohim. Likewise it says (Joshua 4:13): \"about forty thousand armed for battle passed over before YHWH,\" and it says (I Chronicles 22:18): \"and the land shall be subdued before YHWH and before His people\" — now would it enter your mind that Israel subdue the land before the Omnipresent? Rather, all the time they are upon it, it is as though it is subdued; when they are not upon it, it is not subdued. And from this matter they said in Sifrei (Eikev 43): \"and you shall perish quickly\" (Deuteronomy 11:17) — even though I exile you from the Land to outside the Land, be distinguished in the commandments, so that when you return they will not be new to you. A parable: a man who was angry with his wife and sent her away to her father's house. He said to her: adorn yourself with jewels, so that when you return they will not be new upon you. Thus Jeremiah said (31:20): \"Set up signposts for yourself\" — these are the commandments in which Israel are distinguished. Now what Scripture says (Deuteronomy 11:17–18): \"and you shall perish quickly, and you shall place these words of Mine,\" etc., does not obligate in exile except for obligations of the body, such as tefillin and mezuzot, and they explained them as being so that they will not be new upon us when we return to the Land, for the essence of all the commandments is for those dwelling in the land of YHWH. Therefore they said in Sifrei (Re'eh 80): \"and you shall possess it and dwell in it and observe to do\" (Deuteronomy 11:31–32) — dwelling in the land of Israel is weighed against all the commandments in the Torah. And so it is in the Tosefta of Avodah Zarah (ch. 5, hal. 2). This is the calculation of the wicked (Sanhedrin 105a) who used to say to Ezekiel: our master Ezekiel, does a slave whom his master has sold still have any obligation? As it is said (Ezekiel 20:32): \"and what comes into your mind shall not be at all, when you say, We will be like the nations, like the families of the lands, to serve wood and stone.\" And this is the commandment of Jacob our father to his household and to all who were with him at the time of their entry into the Land (Genesis 35:2): \"Remove the strange elohim that are among you and purify yourselves.\" And upon HaShem alone were imputed the circumstances, in that Rachel died on the road at the beginning of their coming into the Land, for in her merit she did not die outside the Land, and in his merit he did not dwell in the Land with two sisters, and she was the one married with the prohibition of a rival wife. It appears that she conceived with Benjamin before their coming to Shechem, and he did not touch her in the Land at all because of the matter we have mentioned. And the prophet said (Jeremiah 16:18): \"and I shall first recompense their iniquity doubly, and their sin, because they have defiled My land with the carcasses of their detestable things and their abominations have filled My inheritance.\" This matter appears in many places in Scripture, and you will see it stated explicitly in them after I have opened your eyes to it. Rabbi Abraham ibn Ezra wrote in the parashah of Vayelekh (Deuteronomy 31:16): we know that HaShem is one, and the difference comes from the recipients, and HaShem does not change His deeds, for all of them are in wisdom; and from the worship of HaShem to maintain the power of reception according to the place, therefore it is written \"the ordinance of the Elohim of the land,\" and He said concerning Jacob \"remove the strange elohim,\" and the reverse is a place attached to forbidden relations, for they are flesh, and המשכיל יבין. These are his words, of blessed memory. Do not answer me from the verse \"Michael, your prince\" (Daniel 10:21), for he is an attending angel appointed to seek mercy for Israel, not a prince of kingdom and dominion. Likewise the officer of the host who appeared to Joshua in Jericho (Joshua 5:13) appeared to him because HaShem sent him to fight their battles, as in the matter of Hezekiah (II Kings 19:35), and also this was while we were outside the Land. And there is no permission to explain the matter of the land more than this, but if you merit to understand the first \"land\" mentioned in the verse of Genesis, and that mentioned in the parashah of \"If in My statutes\" (Leviticus 26:42), you will know a supernal and hidden secret, and you will understand what our Sages said (Tanhuma, Vayakhel 7): the Temple above is established corresponding to the Temple below. And I have already hinted to you in the verse \"for all the earth is Mine\" (Exodus 19:5). Now Scripture mentioned that the men of the land of Canaan were punished because of forbidden relations, and our Sages said (Sanhedrin 56a) that they were warned concerning them from the time of the Creation — to Adam and to Noah — for He does not punish unless He has warned, but Scripture does not mention the warning; rather, it says that the land vomited them out because the land abhors all these abominations. Now it was not only the men of the land of Canaan who were among those warned. The parashah mentioned \"like the deed of the land of Egypt\" (Leviticus 18:3), for they too did all these abominations, and the land of Egypt did not vomit them out, nor did the other lands of the nations vomit out their peoples, but the matter is entirely about the supremacy of the Land and its holiness. And Scripture says (here) \"and the land vomited,\" for from the time He visited its iniquity upon it, when it was decreed upon the Canaanites to be cut off, it is as though it had already vomited them out. Or \"and it vomited\" — upward, as in the matter of \"their shade has departed from upon them\" (Numbers 14:9)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The parenthetical Aramaic phrase (פתגמא ומאמר קדישין שאלתא) appears to be Ramban's own gloss repeating the Aramaic words just quoted from Daniel 4:14; translated hyper-literally as it stands in the text."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:24:51.928352777Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}